WEBVTT

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:03.940
Previously on Smallville.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:05.940
This is all because of Brainiac, isn't it?

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.939
Clark, for once something good came from something horrible.

00:00:08.939 --> 00:00:10.939
I'm choosing to look at this as a gift.

00:00:10.939 --> 00:00:12.939
You have chosen to defy me.

00:00:12.939 --> 00:00:16.940
This defiance cannot go without consequence.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:21.940
Since Jarrell created Brainiac, I think he can cure your infection.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.940
And I think I can recreate Jarrell and the fortress.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.940
I just need to get that crystal back.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.940
All these years of keeping this secret,

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.940
how are you telling me?

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:31.440
I feel like you're telling me.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:32.439
I feel like you were sent to me.

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:34.439
That's great.

00:00:34.439 --> 00:00:38.439
But you don't get how much of my life I spend protecting your secret.

00:00:38.439 --> 00:00:42.229
Chloe, we're done here!

00:00:42.229 --> 00:00:47.229
Chloe's me deep in these situations that humans just don't understand.

00:00:47.229 --> 00:00:50.229
As her best friend, make her stop before she gets hurt.

00:00:50.229 --> 00:00:53.229
Did you help me because of some personal code of ethics,

00:00:53.229 --> 00:00:56.229
or was there more to it than that?

00:00:56.229 --> 00:01:01.820
I think it's best if I don't see you for a while.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:02.820
This will do?

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:03.820
Lois.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:04.819
You don't know who you are.

00:01:04.819 --> 00:01:05.819
You don't know who you are.

00:01:05.819 --> 00:01:07.819
You arrived here as genetic matter,

00:01:07.819 --> 00:01:10.819
containing our planet's most powerful life forms.

00:01:10.819 --> 00:01:16.819
So that in time, you would evolve to become Earth's ultimate destroyer.

00:01:16.819 --> 00:01:19.819
Trust me, my son.

00:01:19.819 --> 00:01:22.819
That which kills you makes you stronger.

00:01:22.819 --> 00:01:38.810
Breakfast in bed for my beautiful bride to be.

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:42.810
I even brewed you a special wedding day countdown, cup of coffee.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:46.810
Two kinds of beans blended together and a tasty marriage of flavor.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:47.810
Oh, well, thank you, too.

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:48.810
Jimmy?

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:49.810
No problem.

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:52.810
It's one week until we rendezvous at the altar,

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:55.810
and we're still getting ours for peace.

00:01:55.810 --> 00:02:00.810
I bet you anything these slow responders have never had to tackle the challenge of a seating shirt.

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:07.219
And one of our invited guests continues to be conspicuously absent.

00:02:07.219 --> 00:02:11.960
Lana?

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:15.340
Who?

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:21.340
A long-time friend, drama with Clark, left town in a hurry, apparently never to be heard from again.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:22.340
Right.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:23.340
Lana.

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.340
I just didn't know.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:26.340
I didn't hear yet.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:29.840
Are you okay?

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.840
Yeah. Why?

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.840
You've been kind of forgetful lately.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.840
Forget the Flores' name one more time.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.840
I think she's gonna stick us with potted ferns.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:42.840
Just distracted.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:45.840
I guess it's a case of the pre-wedding jitters.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:51.610
The hard part?

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:53.610
It's over.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:57.610
Just think of this wedding as one big fiesta to us.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.610
Kind of like the engagement party just with more people.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:06.719
More people.

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:09.719
Let it out, let it in.

00:03:09.719 --> 00:03:12.719
Maybe that we take a little break.

00:03:12.719 --> 00:03:15.719
I thought the whole point of an engagement party was to enjoy the party part.

00:03:15.719 --> 00:03:17.719
I just want two minutes alone with you.

00:03:17.719 --> 00:03:19.719
I've been hugged by so many people today.

00:03:19.719 --> 00:03:21.719
I feel like I'm engaged to everyone but you.

00:03:21.719 --> 00:03:23.719
You're right.

00:03:23.719 --> 00:03:26.719
The night has gone by faster than a flash of a camera wearing, hasn't it?

00:03:26.719 --> 00:03:29.719
Well, that's why we can't miss this dance.

00:03:29.719 --> 00:03:32.719
I love you, Jimmy.

00:03:32.719 --> 00:03:56.000
Jimmy, what's going on?

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.000
This isn't how it happened.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:27.980
What happened?

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:28.980
You okay?

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:29.980
You blink down for a second.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:30.980
You have a headache?

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:32.980
Do you want me to call a doctor?

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:34.980
Get out of my apartment.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:40.980
Louie. It's me. It's Jimmy. It's your fiancé.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.980
I think I'd remember my own fiancee.

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:46.980
I've never seen you before in my life.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:05:51.730
Code right, ZK.

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:53.730
My whole world just fell apart.

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:55.730
Jimmy, slow down. What's going on?

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:59.709
As Chloe's future husband, I thought that I could steer a ship through any

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:05.329
in sickness and in health, but I just got hit with a major bride.

00:06:05.329 --> 00:06:07.329
The wedding's a week away. She's probably just stressed.

00:06:07.329 --> 00:06:10.329
Yeah, that's what I thought, but...

00:06:10.329 --> 00:06:12.329
She's been forgetting things.

00:06:12.329 --> 00:06:16.329
It started out of small stuff, a miss a meeting, a name, a place, that kind of stuff.

00:06:16.329 --> 00:06:20.800
But today, she... she didn't even recognize me.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:23.800
She was actually afraid of me.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:27.560
Did you notice any other symptoms?

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:30.560
Other than the selective amnesia?

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:33.560
Look, she calmed down as soon as I showed a picture of us together,

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:37.810
a picture of us together, but I still don't think that she remembers me.

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:40.810
Chloe, she used to have this medical condition.

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:43.810
I gave her this special ability.

00:06:43.810 --> 00:06:45.810
You mean her meteor ability?

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:47.810
Healing people.

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:50.810
I figure she would have told you, but...

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:52.810
Do you think that it left her with brain damage?

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:53.810
I don't know.

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:55.810
This could be any number of things.

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:58.810
Look, we need to get Chloe through a doctor.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:00.810
Could you talk to her?

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:03.810
Her member may have left me at the altar, but...

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:05.810
She must still remember you.

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:18.970
Excuse me.

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:21.970
Can you tell me how to get to the hospital library?

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:22.970
Are you an intern?

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:23.970
A med student, met you.

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:25.970
Yeah, certainly don't miss those days.

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:27.970
What lucky topic did you take up?

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:30.970
Remember loss, synaptic shock, you know, your basic brain drain.

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:32.970
I was trying to find some information online,

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:35.970
but it looks like most of the cutting-edge research is here at MetGen.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:38.970
Yeah, uh, just down the hall to the east wing, second floor.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:39.970
Thanks. Good luck.

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:45.699
Hey, I, uh, was actually thinking about you.

00:07:45.699 --> 00:07:46.699
Davis, you look exhausted.

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:49.699
Exhausted. You pulling more night after night shifts?

00:07:49.699 --> 00:07:51.699
No, they say it's more like Night of the Living Dead.

00:07:51.699 --> 00:07:55.699
Well, careful that the zombies don't try and eat your brain for breakfast.

00:07:55.699 --> 00:07:57.699
Save yourself. It's a little too late for me.

00:07:57.699 --> 00:08:03.269
I was supposed to look into your past. Davis, I'm...

00:08:03.269 --> 00:08:05.269
You know, my crystal ball is just on the Fritz.

00:08:05.269 --> 00:08:09.269
Actually, I was thinking about it. I'd rather you just cancel the whole sance all together.

00:08:09.269 --> 00:08:12.269
Decided to let the past rest in peace.

00:08:12.269 --> 00:08:15.269
But there's something else. Chloe?

00:08:15.269 --> 00:08:17.269
Something I've been thinking about since the day that we met.

00:08:17.269 --> 00:08:18.269
This is the day that we met.

00:08:18.269 --> 00:08:19.269
You know what, Davis?

00:08:19.269 --> 00:08:21.269
I would really love to hear what you have to say, honestly,

00:08:21.269 --> 00:08:23.269
but now it's just not a good time.

00:08:23.269 --> 00:08:25.269
Got it.

00:08:25.269 --> 00:08:28.269
Is everything okay with you and Jimmy?

00:08:28.269 --> 00:08:31.189
Jimmy?

00:08:31.189 --> 00:08:37.200
Oh, right. Fiancee. Yeah.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:42.080
You've been there for me a lot lately.

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:45.080
If you ever need anything, I'm right here for you.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:51.789
The truth is my brain's just a little fried.

00:08:51.789 --> 00:08:54.789
Literally. I'll talk to you later.

00:08:54.789 --> 00:08:55.789
Of course.

00:08:55.789 --> 00:09:29.210
Chloe, hey, I've been looking all over for you.

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:33.320
for you.

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:35.320
Jimmy says that you're forgetting things,

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:37.320
that this morning you didn't even recognize him.

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:39.320
Jimmy's overreacting.

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:41.320
So you do know who he is?

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:42.320
Of course.

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:46.320
Jimmy Olson, reddish hair, cute smile, photographer,

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:51.309
likes to wear bowling shirts.

00:09:51.309 --> 00:09:54.809
What about fiancee?

00:09:54.809 --> 00:09:55.809
Yeah, right.

00:09:55.809 --> 00:09:58.809
We begin our lives together Saturday at 6.

00:09:58.809 --> 00:10:03.440
Chloe, it sounds like you're reading this all off a list.

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:05.440
Are you sure everything's okay?

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:06.440
I'm just...

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:08.440
distracted, you know?

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:13.879
I mean, last minute wedding plans.

00:10:13.879 --> 00:10:15.879
Why'd you close a bookcase when I walked in?

00:10:15.879 --> 00:10:22.899
Research?

00:10:22.899 --> 00:10:30.210
Client therapist, privilege.

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:31.210
No, Clark.

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:34.210
Please just don't.

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:36.210
Okay?

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:38.210
I'm really busy right now.

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:39.210
I still need to pick the place settings.

00:10:39.210 --> 00:10:42.210
I mean, who knew there were 90 ways to fold the napkin?

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:50.259
Clerk, please!

00:10:50.259 --> 00:10:52.259
Okay, I know this looks a little weird.

00:10:52.259 --> 00:10:54.259
What's going on, Chloe?

00:10:54.259 --> 00:10:59.259
Jimmy's right. I have been drawing a few blanks.

00:10:59.259 --> 00:11:00.259
A few?

00:11:00.259 --> 00:11:05.259
Well, yeah, but I've just been kind of using this as Chloe Sullivan's crib sheet.

00:11:05.259 --> 00:11:09.259
And whenever I forget someone, like you and my fiancé,

00:11:09.259 --> 00:11:12.259
I come here to remind myself of how we're connected.

00:11:12.259 --> 00:11:14.259
Well, listen to what you're saying.

00:11:14.259 --> 00:11:17.259
You had to pace your entire life on these walls.

00:11:17.259 --> 00:11:19.259
There's something seriously wrong with you.

00:11:19.259 --> 00:11:22.279
I still remember you.

00:11:22.279 --> 00:11:30.490
And that's about all I remember.

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:31.490
I've forgotten.

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:35.490
almost everyone, clerk, and I'm having to fake my feelings more and more with people.

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:46.340
Pretty soon there isn't going to be any eye, Chloe, and IQ.

00:11:46.340 --> 00:11:49.340
We both know what's happening to you.

00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:57.679
I'm being taken over by a braniac.

00:11:57.679 --> 00:12:32.309
Davis.

00:12:32.309 --> 00:12:34.309
Hey, Jimmy.

00:12:34.309 --> 00:12:43.659
Uh, Zett, you're RSVP because there's a little thing called a stamp that would have saved this trip.

00:12:43.659 --> 00:12:47.659
Um, I'm sorry, I can't stick around and Chloe's not here, so...

00:12:47.659 --> 00:12:49.659
Yeah, I ran into her in the city.

00:12:49.659 --> 00:12:51.659
Your name came up and she acted kind of weird...

00:12:51.659 --> 00:12:53.659
a weird. Is everything okay?

00:12:53.659 --> 00:12:57.659
Yeah, sure, no. It's just a little temporary detour on her way down the aisle.

00:12:57.659 --> 00:13:02.759
You really...

00:13:02.759 --> 00:13:05.759
love her. Don't you?

00:13:05.759 --> 00:13:09.759
Yeah. Like Sinatra said.

00:13:09.759 --> 00:13:13.759
She's all I long for. All I worship and adore her.

00:13:13.759 --> 00:13:16.399
You know what I mean?

00:13:16.399 --> 00:13:23.360
Yeah, I do. I do. I do.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:26.360
I'm just sorry that I won't be able to make it.

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:31.360
Oh. Well, unlike some of my extended family, I'm not going to enjoy

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:33.360
and your reply card on the regrets pile.

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:36.360
Oh, no, I'm sorry that I won't be there,

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:38.360
but could you do me a favor?

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:41.360
Would you mind just telling Chloe for me?

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:43.360
Yeah, yeah, no, that's no problem.

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:53.360
She's an amazing girl.

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:54.360
Take care of her.

00:13:54.360 --> 00:14:06.879
Brainiac's always got an objective.

00:14:06.879 --> 00:14:08.879
Chloe, do you remember anything from this morning

00:14:08.879 --> 00:14:10.879
when you lost your last memory of Jimmy?

00:14:10.879 --> 00:14:12.879
Every time I try and think about someone that I've forgotten,

00:14:12.879 --> 00:14:15.879
it's like this swarm of cryptonian symbols that I don't understand.

00:14:15.879 --> 00:14:18.879
It's like times square times 100 in my head.

00:14:18.879 --> 00:14:19.879
Brainiac is replacing your...

00:14:19.879 --> 00:14:21.879
memories with Kryptonian data.

00:14:21.879 --> 00:14:24.879
Yeah, and this one keeps repeating itself over and over again.

00:14:24.879 --> 00:14:31.240
This is a symbol for doom.

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:33.240
Do you think Brainiac is sending me a message?

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:36.240
Whatever he's doing, Chloe, we need to stop it.

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:40.240
Jerell created Brainiac. When Kara lost her memory, Jarrell restored.

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:44.240
If I take the crystal to the Arctic and rebuild the fortress,

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:45.240
Jerome might be able to help you too.

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:49.240
Or he could strip you of your powers or drop an ice castle on you.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:51.240
Doesn't matter, Chloe.

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:52.240
I have to do this.

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:53.240
And I have to be honest with you, Clark. This is a lot.

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:55.240
I'm honest with you, Clark, this is exactly why I didn't tell you

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:57.240
what was happening with me.

00:14:57.240 --> 00:14:59.240
Because I knew that you would just fly off

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:01.240
without thinking about any of the consequences.

00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:02.240
Clark, last time you handled this crystal,

00:15:02.240 --> 00:15:05.240
exact you to the Phantom Zone.

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:07.240
Now, for all we know, Lex could have sent this to you.

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:09.240
I mean, he could still be trying to control you

00:15:09.240 --> 00:15:10.240
from wherever he is.

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:13.240
Chloe, none of this would have happened

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:15.240
if you hadn't tried to protect me.

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:17.240
Everyone who knows about my secret,

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:20.240
I've watched him either go away or die.

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:22.240
My dad, Pete.

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:25.240
Lana, Lionel, even Lex.

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:31.279
Chloe, I'm not going to let my secret destroy your life, too.

00:15:31.279 --> 00:15:35.279
The night that I saw you catch that car with your bare hands, it changed my life.

00:15:35.279 --> 00:15:37.279
For the better.

00:15:37.279 --> 00:15:40.279
Clark, thanks to you, I've actually made an impact on the world.

00:15:40.279 --> 00:15:43.279
I wouldn't trade that for anything.

00:15:43.279 --> 00:15:52.090
Chloe?

00:15:52.090 --> 00:16:16.419
Chloe!

00:16:16.419 --> 00:16:17.419
Chloe!

00:16:17.419 --> 00:16:21.850
Chloe, snap down it.

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:27.710
Chloe, hey, Chloe, Chloe, you okay?

00:16:27.710 --> 00:16:28.710
Yeah, my head just feels like a voli.

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:31.710
It feels like a volleyball at the Summer Olympics.

00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:32.710
You blacked out again.

00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:35.210
Come on.

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:36.210
Let's sit down.

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:41.509
Did you lose another memory?

00:16:41.509 --> 00:16:44.509
I think you snapped me out of it before anything completely disappeared.

00:16:44.509 --> 00:16:56.299
I guess the more I think about someone, the more my memory gives them a complete mental makeover.

00:16:56.299 --> 00:17:00.299
Before you trailed off, you were talking about the first time you saw me use my abilities.

00:17:00.299 --> 00:17:01.299
Abilities?

00:17:01.299 --> 00:17:08.839
Is in your ability to look both ways before you cross the street?

00:17:08.839 --> 00:17:10.819
Clark, all I remember is hiding behind some

00:17:10.839 --> 00:17:14.839
instruction equipment and watching you stand in the middle of the road.

00:17:14.839 --> 00:17:17.839
You don't remember an out-of-control car?

00:17:17.839 --> 00:17:22.460
Were you hit by a car that night?

00:17:22.460 --> 00:17:29.490
I thought I'm starting to lose things about you too now.

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:36.579
Do you remember the name Kellel?

00:17:36.579 --> 00:17:38.859
Should I?

00:17:38.859 --> 00:17:40.859
What about Krypton or Brainiac?

00:17:40.859 --> 00:17:41.859
Brainiac?

00:17:41.859 --> 00:17:43.859
Brainiac. People used to call me that when I was a kid.

00:17:43.859 --> 00:17:46.880
Right?

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:52.940
What? I'm forgetting something important now.

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:54.940
What don't I remember?

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:59.890
Look, Clark, this isn't going to stop.

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:01.890
I'm losing everything.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:05.880
Chloe, it's gonna be okay.

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:07.880
But I need you to trust me.

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:11.880
I know someone who can help us, but you need to stay here and relax and I'll talk to them.

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:14.880
No, Clark. Don't call, please, don't leave me.

